Wayfindr is set up.

  Config        <root>/config/wayfindr/wayfindr.toml (created)
  Data dir      <root>/data/wayfindr
  Master key    OS keychain
  Client token  <root>/data/wayfindr/client-token (created)

Add a connector
---------------

  wayfindr connector add linear --url https://mcp.linear.app/mcp
  wayfindr connector add fs -- npx -y @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem ~/src

The command asks an HTTP server whether it uses OAuth and offers to
authorize it. wayfindr status shows every connector's state.

Connect a client
----------------

Add Wayfindr to your harness with the stdio shim (wayfindr stdio). The shim
reads the client token itself and starts the daemon if it is not running.
It needs wayfindr on the harness's PATH.

Claude Code: run
  claude mcp add --scope user --transport stdio wayfindr -- wayfindr stdio

Codex: run
  codex mcp add wayfindr -- wayfindr stdio

OpenCode: run
  opencode mcp add --global wayfindr -- wayfindr stdio

Hermes Agent: run
  hermes mcp add wayfindr --command wayfindr --args stdio

Gemini CLI: run
  gemini mcp add --scope user wayfindr wayfindr stdio

GitHub Copilot CLI: run
  copilot mcp add wayfindr -- wayfindr stdio

VS Code: run
  code --add-mcp '{"name":"wayfindr","type":"stdio","command":"wayfindr","args":["stdio"]}'

Cursor: add to ~/.cursor/mcp.json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "wayfindr": { "type": "stdio", "command": "wayfindr", "args": ["stdio"] }
  }
}

Zed: add to settings.json
{
  "context_servers": {
    "wayfindr": { "command": "wayfindr", "args": ["stdio"] }
  }
}

Windsurf (Devin Desktop): add to ~/.config/devin/mcp_config.json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "wayfindr": { "command": "wayfindr", "args": ["stdio"] }
  }
}

goose: add to ~/.config/goose/config.yaml
extensions:
  wayfindr:
    type: stdio
    name: wayfindr
    cmd: wayfindr
    args: [stdio]
    enabled: true
    timeout: 300

To connect over HTTP instead (http://127.0.0.1:7777/mcp), start the daemon
(wayfindr start) and set the client token where the harness runs:

  export WAYFINDR_CLIENT_TOKEN="$(cat '<root>/data/wayfindr/client-token')"

HTTP setup for each harness: https://atomicpages.github.io/wayfindr/guide/clients

Usage telemetry is off by default. To send the maintainers an anonymous
daily usage report, set enabled = true under [telemetry] in the config.
What it holds: https://atomicpages.github.io/wayfindr/reference/telemetry
